# Pavilion vs SHMS deploys

Build **Pavilion** as if SHMS never existed (product, tenants, `onpavilion.com`, demo/trials). No Stone Hill PII or school cost on Pavilion.

Stone Hill (`frontend` / www.shmspto.org) and Pavilion apps (`commons-pto-demo`, `commons-pto`, `commons-site`) share this monorepo for now but are **separate products**.

Application ships follow **Staging-first** in `ship-after-serena.mdc` (critical, every agent):

1. Serena QA → commit task files only (no push yet).
2. **Staging** deploy of the **target product(s) for that task** from a **clean worktree of that SHA**. Never `--prod` yet. Never deploy from a dirty tree.
   Stone Hill → alias to **https://shmspto.vercel.app** (not ephemeral Preview URLs). Prefer `node scripts/deploy-staging.mjs --cwd <worktree>`.
3. **STOP.** Give Rob https://shmspto.vercel.app. Wait for explicit OK.
4. After OK: promote / `--prod`, **then** push GitHub.

Staff-only exception (Staff UI / `/api/staff` / staff permissions with no visitor UI change): commit → staging **and** prod from the same SHA (no Rob wait) → push. Details in `ship-after-serena.mdc`.
5. **If you shipped Stone Hill** and the change could improve the Pavilion platform: **ask Rob** whether to also stage (then prod) Pavilion (`commons-pto-demo` and/or `commons-pto`) from the same SHA. Do **not** auto-deploy Pavilion on every SHMS ship.
6. If the task is Pavilion-only (`commons-site`, demo vanillaize, trial packs), ship Pavilion projects only (same staging → OK → prod → push). Do not require a Stone Hill deploy.

Never put Stone Hill `DATABASE_URL` / Wix / Square env on Pavilion projects, or Pavilion `DATABASE_URL` / Stripe on Stone Hill.

At session start: `node scripts/commons-parity.mjs` is informational. Do not force catch-up unless Rob wants Pavilion on that SHA or the task is Pavilion-facing.

Plaid stays on the **Trial** account until paying Pavilion clients.

Vanillaize / demo gates still apply on Commons demo. After a Pavilion-facing ship, run `node scripts/commons-surface-check.mjs`.
